sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as MCP client
    participant MCP as Scene tool adapter
    participant Policy as Capability policy
    participant HTTP as Bridge HTTP adapter
    participant Service as Scene override service
    participant Live as song.scenes[index]

    Client->>MCP: tools/list or tools/call
    MCP->>Policy: Resolve active bridge routes
    Policy-->>MCP: Supported, conditional, or fail-closed

    alt Read-only capability request
        MCP->>HTTP: GET /scenes/tempo-signature-capabilities?sceneIndex=N
        HTTP->>Service: Inspect exact index
        Service->>Live: Read fields and inspect descriptors
        Live-->>Service: Fresh observable snapshot
        Service-->>HTTP: Target, capabilities, normalized and raw observations
        HTTP-->>MCP: 200 JSON; zero setters
    else Set or clear request
        MCP->>MCP: Validate exact tagged actions and bounds
        MCP->>HTTP: POST /scenes/tempo-signature-overrides
        HTTP->>Service: Validate again and resolve exact index
        Service->>Live: Capture complete pre-state and capability matrix
        Service->>Service: Preflight all requested families
        loop Ordered non-no-op setters
            Service->>Service: Journal setter before invocation
            Service->>Live: Write value before enable
        end
        Service->>Live: Reacquire song.scenes[index] and read back
        alt Exact target and value verification
            Service-->>HTTP: 200 changed or no-op result
        else Setter, resolution, readback, or mismatch failure
            loop Journal entries in reverse order
                Service->>Live: Reacquire exact index and compensate
            end
            Service->>Live: Reacquire and verify full observable pre-state
            Service-->>HTTP: Structured transaction and rollback error
        end
        HTTP-->>MCP: JSON result or preserved error details
    end

    Note over Service,Live: Never launch a scene or write Song tempo, Arrangement automation, clips, or transport.
